title: Shared abilities, nothing, and kinds of problems
card: Chapter 13 | Shared abilities | Different things that can do the same thing
say:
  A dog and a robot are different kinds of things. But both can speak. Fathom can keep them together, as things that can speak.
uncard

new: speakers.fathom
type fast:
  a speaker is anything that can speak.

  a dog has:
    name (text)
  and the universe said i love you

  a robot has:
    model (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  to speak, for a dog, returning text:
    return "Woof, I'm [name]"
  and the universe said i love you

  to speak, for a robot, returning text:
    return "Beep, model [model]"
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    conjure a dog as rex
    set the name of rex to "Rex"
    conjure a robot as unit
    set the model of unit to 7
    set talkers to a list of speakers
    add rex to talkers
    add unit to talkers
    for each t in talkers:
      scrawl speak t
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: line 1
spot: line 1
say:
  A speaker is anything that can speak. That one line makes a new kind: any kind of thing with its own speak command is a speaker.
zoom: lines 11-17
spot: lines 11-13
say: A dog speaks its own way.
spot: lines 15-17
say: And a robot speaks another.
zoom: lines 19-29
spot: lines 24-26
say: A list of speakers holds the dog and the robot together.
spot: lines 27-28
say: And speak does the speaking the way each kind of thing does it, found while the program runs.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 13 | Nothing | When there isn't one
say:
  Sometimes a command looks for something, and doesn't find it. A name for a kind of thing can hold nothing.
uncard
new: nothing.fathom
type fast:
  an enemy has:
    health (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  to the weakest, given enemies (a list of enemys), returning an enemy:
    set best to no enemy
    for each e in enemies:
      if best is nothing or the health of e falls below the health of best:
        set best to e
    return best
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    set nobody to a list of enemys
    set found to the weakest with nobody
    if found is nothing:
      scrawl "No enemies left!"
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 5-10
spot: line 6
say: Set best to no enemy: best holds nothing, for now.
spot: line 8
say: If best is nothing, there's no best yet, so this enemy is the best so far.
zoom: lines 13-17
spot: lines 14-17
say:
  Given an empty list, the weakest finds nothing, and the program can ask: is it nothing? Asking for a part of nothing stops the program, with a message that says so.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 13 | Kinds of problems | Catching only some mistakes
say:
  In chapter eight, try caught every problem. A problem can also have a kind of its own, named in your own words, and be caught on its own.
uncard
new: fuel.fathom
type fast:
  to drive, given fuel (a number):
    if fuel is 0: raise a fuel problem with "the tank is empty"
    if fuel exceeds 100: raise an error with "that's too much fuel"
    scrawl "Driving with ", fuel
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    for each f in a list of (50, 0, 500):
      try:
        drive with f
      if that went wrong with a fuel problem:
        scrawl "Fuel problem: ", the wound
      if that went wrong:
        scrawl "Some other problem: ", the wound
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-4
spot: line 2
say: Raise a fuel problem: a kind of problem, named in our own words.
spot: line 3
say: Raise an error is a plain problem.
zoom: lines 7-14
spot: lines 11-12
say: If that went wrong with a fuel problem takes only fuel problems.
spot: lines 13-14
say: And a plain if that went wrong, last, takes the rest.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out
